  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Crozius Arcanum" id="2927-357a-fc6c-42c3" hidden="false">
      <description>Uses Power Weapon profile</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rosarius" id="479f-929d-b531-a315" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 4+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Terminator Honors" id="bad9-31ae-7a9c-f38c" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain +1 Attack (Already included for Veteran Sergeants and Space Marines wearing Terminator Armour)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bionics" id="93ed-72da-0689-8a2d" hidden="false">
      <description>If a model with bionics is killed, instead of removing it, place it on its side. Roll a D6 at the start of the next turn; on a roll of a 6 the model stands back up with 1 wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Artificer Armor" id="7a02-cc04-9d97-3493" hidden="false">
      <description>Upgrades Power Armour to a 2+</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Purity Seals" id="8fca-253c-bbf8-9510" hidden="false">
      <description>When a unit including a model wearing Purity Seals falls back, roll one extra D6 for the fall back distance, and then pick the D6 results you want.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Iron Halo" id="c214-19e6-edea-0f81" hidden="false">
      <description>The iron halo grants a 4+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Auspex" id="00e2-88f3-119d-9df3" hidden="false">
      <description>If enemy infiltrators set up within 4D6&quot; of a model with a auspex, then that model and the unit they are attached to is allowed to take a &quot;free&quot; shot at them. These shots are taken before the battle begins and may cause the infiltrators to fall back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Psychic Hood" id="d637-ddb3-5ed3-bee8" hidden="false">
      <description>Declare you&apos;ll use the Psychic Hood after an opponent has successfully made a Psychic test, but before they have resolved the power. Each player rolls a D6 and adds their respective model&apos;s Leadership value. If the Space Marine beats the opposing model&apos;s score then the psychic power is nullified and may not be used that turn. Otherwise the power is unaffected. The Hood may be used each time an enemy model uses a power.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="And They Shall Know No Fear" id="7097-810b-2462-51cb" hidden="false">
      <description>Space Marines automatically regroup as they fall back, even if the squad is reduced to less than 50% by casualties, but not if the squad is out of coherency or there are enemy models within 6&quot;. If the enemy advance into them the Space Marines are not destroyed and the new assault is treated in the same way as a sweeping advance (enemy gaining +1 A next turn).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drop Pods" id="e75a-c8bc-ad0d-01af" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of a battle where the mission allows Deep Strike, the Space Marines may choose to deploy using Drop Pods instead of deploying like normal. Models doing this will deploy using the Deep Strike rules. Only the following can deploy from Drop Pods. All other units must sit out the mission: Marines in Power Armour or Terminator Armour; Scouts; Dreadnoughts and Land Speeders.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Chapter Banner" id="5df3-0068-e083-9213" hidden="false">
      <description>Add +1 to the Space Marine combat resolution socre of any assault that takes place within 6&quot; of the Chapter Banner. Additionally, once per game the banner may be activated to grant all Space Marines within 2D6&quot; to gain +1 Attack for the rest of the turn. Note it may be activated during the enemy&apos;s turn.
However, if the model bearing the standard is slain in close combat, then the enemy model that slew him captures the standard gains the +1 bonus to combat resolution from then on. It is possible for the model to change hands multiple times per game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Holy Relic" id="a3b0-6af2-1358-7196" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game the relic may be activated to grant all Space Marines within 2D6&quot; to gain +1 Attack for the rest of the turn. Note it may be activated during the enemy&apos;s turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Narthecium" id="cfad-88c2-ae81-cdc1" hidden="false">
      <description>The Narthecium allows the medic to ignore the first failed saving throw each turn in the unit containing the Apothecary. This may not be used on any model who suffered &apos;Instant Death&apos; or hit by a weapon that allows no saves. It cannot be used if the Apothecary is in base to base contact with an enemy model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Reductor" id="ba6f-5067-ce85-aa4b" hidden="false">
      <description>At the end of a scenario that uses Victory Points, gain 1 VP per slain Space Marine as long as the Apothecary is alive at the end of the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sacred Standard" id="66ac-c870-a383-6b83" hidden="false">
      <description>Add +1 to the Space Marine combat resolution socre of any assault that takes place within 6&quot; of the Sacred Banner.
However, if the model bearing the standard is slain in close combat, then the enemy model that slew him captures the standard gains the +1 bonus to combat resolution from then on. It is possible for the model to change hands multiple times per game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Signum" id="9ba6-c94b-3548-d9e8" hidden="false">
      <description>Each turn, you may re-roll one missed to hit shooting dice for the Command squad the Techmarine belongs to.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Teleport Homer" id="250f-507f-ea1b-b164" hidden="false">
      <description>If the template used by teleporting Terminators making a Deep Strike is centered  on the model with the homer, then it does not scatter.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Terminator Armour" id="fe7a-62df-712a-5bc5" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 2+ Armour save and 5+ invulnerable save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dozer Blade" id="9d15-603e-4af4-bf3f" hidden="false">
      <description>Re-roll failed Difficult Terrain tests as long as the model did not move more than 6&quot; that turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Extra Armour" id="8921-da68-8172-a6a5" hidden="false">
      <description>Treat &apos;Crew Stunned&apos; results as &apos;Crew Shaken&apos; instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Searchlight" id="cdf1-af4d-b6a8-3a2a" hidden="false">
      <description>During battles using Night Fight rules, one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle may be fired at by all other friendly units within range and that have line of sight, but by doing so the vehicle may be fired at by all enemy units in the next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Smoke Launchers" id="42cc-b2d9-b9f3-90ea" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, after completing its move, a vehicle with Smoke Launchers may trigger them. The vehicle may not fire this turn, but any penetrating hits scored by the enemy in the next shooting phase are instead turned into glancing hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Death Mask" id="c585-ce6a-bf8d-27a5" hidden="false">
      <description>Any enemy unit that loses as close combat against a model wearing a Death Mask suffers -1 modifier to its Leadership test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Exsanguinator" id="3043-42d1-b30e-28e4" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows attached squad to ignore first failed armor save each turn, but subsequent saves are negated on a D6 roll less than or equal to the bearer&apos;s Toughness. If higher, the bearer and failing models are wounded with no armor save allowed. (Does not negate instant death and cannot be used when in base-to-base contact)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grail" id="d463-2905-bcde-0a33" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Blood Angels unit with a model within 6&quot; of a character with a Grail may roll an extra dice when making an advance after winning a close combat and discard the lowest.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Holy Shroud" id="1d4a-2b4c-e8a4-8d7d" hidden="false">
      <description>Ignores negative Leadership modifiers for all units within 6&quot;</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Lion Helm" id="6deb-edba-53ca-53b5" hidden="false">
      <description>Carried by helmet bearer within 2&quot; of unit. Grants 4+ invulnerable save to all models (including enemies) within 3&quot; against shooting attacks</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sword of Secrets" id="73fd-818d-e387-e703" hidden="false">
      <description>Power weapon, but can also be used with a Strength of 6</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Book of Salvation" id="38a3-2029-a26a-69de" hidden="false">
      <description>If the bearer is slain, place the model on it&apos;s side. Any Dark Angels within 6&quot; must move to retrieve the book. Until recovered, all Space Marines become Stubborn, if not already, all may ignore the &quot;Intractable&quot; special rule, and all add +1 to Weapon Skill. If the Book is not retrieved by the end of the battle, the Space Marines lose the game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blades of Reason" id="7177-bf98-d1f1-c06b" hidden="false">
      <description>If the bearer survives to the end of the mission, roll a D6 for each enemy model slain. On a 6, they are captured adding +D6 Victory Points. (Cannot be used against Necrons or Tyranids)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Cup of Retribution" id="eb88-3b95-a020-38c0" hidden="false">
      <description>All Space Marines within 2D6&quot; gain +1 Attack bonus for the rest of the turn when revealed</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Standard of Devastation" id="2925-28e3-33e7-101b" hidden="false">
      <description>Add +1 to the Space Marine combat resolution score of any assault that takes place within 6&quot; of the Sacred Banner.
However, if the model bearing the standard is slain in close combat, then the enemy model that slew him captures the standard gains the +1 bonus to combat resolution from then on. It is possible for the model to change hands multiple times per game.


In addition, one unit with a model within 6&quot; can shoot during the opponent&apos;s Assault Phase once per-battle</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Standard of Fortitude" id="061d-26d8-4ad2-d2dc" hidden="false">
      <description>Add +1 to the Space Marine combat resolution score of any assault that takes place within 6&quot; of the Sacred Banner.
However, if the model bearing the standard is slain in close combat, then the enemy model that slew him captures the standard gains the +1 bonus to combat resolution from then on. It is possible for the model to change hands multiple times per game.


In addition, one unit with a model within 6&quot; can use rapid fire weapons after moving once per-battle</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Standard of Retribution" id="f403-bb3d-e854-1b24" hidden="false">
      <description>Add +1 to the Space Marine combat resolution score of any assault that takes place within 6&quot; of the Sacred Banner.
However, if the model bearing the standard is slain in close combat, then the enemy model that slew him captures the standard gains the +1 bonus to combat resolution from then on. It is possible for the model to change hands multiple times per game.


In addition, one unit with a model within 6&quot; can re-roll any failed Assault hit rolls once per-battle</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stubborn" id="1eb7-6961-7e16-d0b6" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit will automatically pass any Morale checks they have to take, even if faced by a situation or opponent that would normally cause them to automatically fail. Note that they still must test for pinning as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Salamanders Mantle" id="fced-61c2-a13a-ca80" hidden="false">
      <description>The character is immune to suffering instant death caused by being hit by an attack which has a Strength value double his Toughness. The character loses a single wound instead. Note that instant death can be suffered in other ways.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Storm Shield" id="9bbf-cb2e-4a41-dd4b" hidden="false">
      <description>Allows a 4+ invulnerable save against one opponent per turn in close combat. Cannot be combined with Rosarius or Iron Halo saves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Over-charged Engine" id="cf39-fe5b-7f74-8313" hidden="false"/>
    <rule name="Boarding Shield" id="e6cf-92a2-fe08-ae07" hidden="false">
      <comment>Badab War Item</comment>
      <description>Confers a 5+ Invulnerable Save, but always takes up one hand in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Combat Shield" id="52d5-5595-9603-6eba" hidden="false">
      <comment>Badab War Item</comment>
      <description>Confers a 6+ Invulnerable save, but does not use any hands.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Refractor Field" id="74c9-0d87-cc34-17c7" hidden="false">
      <description>5+ Invulnerable Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dark Harvest" id="d9fe-e333-7e7f-a280" hidden="false">
      <description>For a Corpse-Taker, in addition to its normal rules, the Reductor also gains 3 VP for each enemy Space Marine slain within 6&quot; of the Corpse-Taker, as long as the Corpse-Taker is alive at the end of the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Target-Primus" id="9ba7-5182-873c-0b52" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Corpse-Taker is slain in close combat, award half of the Dark-Harvest victory points (rounding up) to the opposing player instead.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
