        <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="e6d5-bc03-5827-d5da" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="0"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
        <modifier field="error" type="add" value="can only be in a force of 1500 points or more.">
          <conditionGroups>
            <conditionGroup type="and">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="f98d-e661-a9b7-39af" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="atLeast" value="1"/>
                <condition childId="any" field="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="1500"/>
              </conditions>
            </conditionGroup>
          </conditionGroups>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Banner of Macragge" id="3f7b-1756-1f02-d414" hidden="false" page="120" publicationId="26e5-ce39-9a6e-4817">
          <description>The Banner of Macragge has the combined effect of both the Sacred Standard and Holy Relic. In addition, Ancient Helveticus and any Ultramarines squad he joins becomes fearless and automatically passes any Morale or Pinning checks that they have to take. Even effects that normally force a fall back move to take place with no Morale check are ignored by Helveticus and the unit.


Finally, the presences of the Banner of Macragge is an unwelcome sight to their enemies - it tells them that they are facing the entire might of the Chapter. This is represented by all enemy units with 12&quot; of the banner bearing suffering -1 to their Leadership values for any Morale checks they are forced to make. 


If Ancient Helveticus is killed, these benefits no longer apply for whoever picks up the banner. Also these benefits do not apply if Ancient Helveticus is inside of a vehicle, bunker or off-table in reserve.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Foresworn" id="4b07-bed3-cb83-ea7a" hidden="false" page="120" publicationId="26e5-ce39-9a6e-4817">
          <description>Ancient Helventicus&apos; armour save counts as being invulnerable.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Protect the Flag!" id="3f35-a0a9-baae-638b" hidden="false" page="120" publicationId="26e5-ce39-9a6e-4817">
          <description>If Ancient Helveticus is killed, leave the model in place to show where the banner has fallen. Regardless of the mission being played, the Ultramarine player now also has to full the victory conditions for a &apos;Rescue&apos; standard mission, treating the sadly departed Helveticus as the objective. If the Ultramarine player is not in possession of the banner at the end of the battle, they lose regardless of any other victory conditions. If they have the banner, they only win if they have fulfilled the victory conditions of the original mission as well.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
